{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:03b5522134c00187a39d258af46e7286e884ba4ba82d42e6ecfb3423c3d8605a","title":"What photon signal follows if a surviving light modulus is a subcomponent of Galactic and cosmological dark matter? The abundance and spatial distribution are phenomenological inputs rather than outputs of the proposed early-universe dilution.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03e2016057e759a07fd15c21c84c0911e3d6d6c5f3e5f486e63901665eb3f93d","title":"Can a broken additional gauge interaction provide Higgs quartic corrections while its vector multiplet is integrated out?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:037a24e1c2d1f0436bc5ca0765a902ef9fe98be0050092ec7779bd218aecb3d3","title":"Which combinations of quantum corrections and additional sources can stabilize Kähler moduli while preserving a controlled large-volume expansion? The appendix compares mechanisms by their competing potential terms, flux-superpotential magnitude, topology, and gauge-sector assumptions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:033bb47198fa62b2b6ee453d6c92e7323c4c7d806af26758d30a3b14439e9bfa","title":"Can summing closed-string tree diagrams with NS–NS tadpoles recover physical vacuum energies when calculations start from a background that fails the field equations? The paper tests a boundary-state prescription against bosonic tachyon condensation and orientifold examples.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03d799ab12e96ae32b7906cee2db50fa06ba9a0df351aa0be4b9a79f245e9ee0","title":"Can B2 and C2 axions in type IIB orientifolds with h1,1− ≠ 0 be stabi