s and Hubble rates?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03394bf20ceebe5d8fa665d97dfd6b5e900d27627f13bc5286f807cfb8cacd4f","title":"What do axilaton deformations imply about 3+1-dimensional de Sitter backgrounds in string theory, their supersymmetric limits and duality patching, and the need for string degrees of freedom beyond a tree-level spacetime effective description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:033ec0e5a0f73f270fe2a7cb7bb455c0e48291bb3db13e0099be36fbf7308432","title":"This ansatz isolates whether an exactly de Sitter external metric can coexist with a static compactification and controlled corrections. Its uplift translates late conformal time into a small type IIA coupling.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:032417b11a93e7e54228b390e3a1ed7e943d3e1503dc0de6fc8348c5d468c170","title":"Can a holographic composite axion retain its QCD coupling while sufficiently suppressing gravitational PQ violation through separation between an IR-localized axion and UV sources of explicit breaking?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0331d936c08069563803cebe5d3527498080bf62848a27ba3f499deb4eb96d33","title":"Why do perturbative string compactifications so often yield no-scale supergravity, and which quantum or α′ corrections first lift its flat potentials? The authors seek symmetry-based constraints that assess the robustness of moduli stabilization and explain classical de Sitter obstructions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0054"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03840f73db06753d87ff1683c8f2e0df49f0b514a22a030c1a710a6012b0553b","title":"Which scalar trajectories satisfy the adopted quantum-gravity conjectures? The paper imposes an order-one excursion limit and a slope-or-negative-curvature condition, using the slope branch to test inflation on a positive linear potential.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03ca34b4576ed2459d32cf34eff2b9fd393e2c1eb0d47b1e59d3a8911f07c9ec","title":"How does the competition between explicit and spontaneous spacetime-symmetry breaking change the low-energy collective modes of holographic fluids and solids? The window compares transverse and longitudinal pole spectra, including pseudo-phonons, relaxation, and sound–diffusion interactions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03a23c4d6ca92b6dfcf7d9a416ec48dd6ee1e51753fab28517a12ab4e37a66b9","title":"Does the large-complex-structure quintic spectrum approach a three-sphere base spectrum under torus collapse?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03e3b8213f1d565e19b034a4d6601ab7cbb2c1389399e42907479043c6d7c99a","title":"Can separately measuring rotation of reionization and recombination CMB polarization produce a calibration-independent birefringence observable and constrain when the responsible new physics acted?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0381e377d66fc5cb3c3dcd4eab33a6df90ce808ef1b989c355f3b43d4d72641e","title":"Which internal geometry and units underlie the spectral branches? The calculation fixes Einstein squashing, Ricci curvature 27/10, and |m|=3/(2sqrt(5)) in dimensionless units, while retaining the flux sign for the later compactification.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03bd9a53345f7e8fa4d36e540cb2a798e271a8e3295085231f3569ffdf59e672","title":"The setting isolates how an independently varied gravitational connection changes the canonical Higgs inflation potential and its refined-dS diagnostics. The analysis keeps a single scalar and freezes the non-minimal coupling xi.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0071"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03950d9098490d9c17e92c415ade5959bbae76dab4c8e83576b2700b261b0010","title":"What changes when the three-dimensional tensor component of a circle-compactified four-dimensional metric varies along the circle? The paper studies this dependence in Einstein gravity coupled to Standard Model matter rather than discarding it in the reduction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0334476ae9bdc3c6912b9e27fe1325f676c81673457496e7f0744882b5ebec3e","title":"Can exceptional-divisor data and cobordism compensation recover or constrain ADE singularities and the gauge groups associated with defect-sourced fluxes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0077"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03a019ea2214c6351dd4d158df5bc5c4d751dfd5cabc7edb2b0368d3c9a2cdd5","title":"Can string orbifolding be formulated through spacetime gauge symmetries and consistency conditions, treating all dynamical objects equally, despite the conjectural absence of global symmetries in quantum gravity? Can its possible outcomes be independent of duality frame?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0077"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03dcea30b48af9ba78b79bfadb7dac039d0387de56da65eb5126f015b967483a","title":"Must local higher-derivative corrections dominate nonlocal quantum corrections outside large extremal black holes, and what would this 