er mid-redshift and weaker recent acceleration indicated by the paper's distance-data interpretation, including crossing w=-1, while avoiding unacceptable changes to matter and structure growth?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0094"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:033c61b7f5495aadaba46ad97bb95ed6785a0997bf9dd85b475b6a2e4d612d81","title":"Can birational geometry produce explicit, uniform upper bounds on the multiplet spectrum of six-dimensional N=(1,0) gravity, beginning with tensor multiplets, and give these bounds a bottom-up interpretation conditional on physical conjectures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0095"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:039d64e67df4cdc89af69f2743b3070e7701bd7be146bf3cfc336d171dadb3ea","title":"Which leading effective interactions between Standard Model and hidden-sector matter are actually generated by tree-level and one-loop gravity, and what follows for dimension-five portals, ultralight scalar dark matter and matter symmetries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0098"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0337682f4686898ff87b6fc468ea7157e574658f326a2c323af535e061dd822c","title":"Do anomaly cancellation, gauge-enhancement singularities and higher-dimensional limits uniquely constrain the BPS protected couplings of eight-dimensional minimal supergravity with two vector multiplets, and exclude a gravitational contribution to the H-flux Bianchi identity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0100"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:03c3afe1831a3529f54ba5f65a192ff04e9bcbe67b21088b56d6ff5a7bc88fba","title":"Can observers actively probe nontrivial spacetime topology using causal signals arriving from past null infinity and returning to future null infinity? The paper seeks sufficient causal and energy hypotheses forbi